  m_text: "Life is inherently unsatisfying, but the origin of SUFFERING lies in our
    insatiable DESIRES for pleasure. In turn, desire arises from IGNORANCE of the
    true nature of reality. \nUncontrolled desire leads to ATTACHMENT, which, when
    confronted with the impermanence of things, produces suffering."
